      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that in ischemic stroke SD is observed as peri-infarct depolarizations and can drive infarct expansion into penumbral areas, but it does not support the claim that in hemorrhagic stroke “SD is part of the secondary injury process linked to later cerebral ischemia.” The packet mentions secondary injury and delayed cerebral ischemia, but it does not explicitly link SD to that secondary-injury mechanism in hemorrhagic stroke.",
        "The packet does not explicitly support the phrasing that SD is “often seen after stroke” (it specifically states it is frequently observed in ischemic stroke, but does not clearly generalize across stroke types as “often seen after stroke”)."
